{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1494860-using-1ed-to-try-out-the-setting","id":1494860,"title":"Using 1ed to try out the setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-12T05:53:24-07:00","id":1494860,"title":"Using 1ed to try out the setting","content":"My group never really explored NWOD/COD after the OWOD ended. Over the years I did collect the majority of the WtF 1ed books as well as the other games. I want to run short campaigns for each of the COD settings to try them out. For WtF what books would you suggest to really focus on for a 1ed game? How useful is the Hunting Ground Rockies book in particular or the old demo campaign? As for 2ed, I have checked it out and system wise it's not my thing so I plan on using the 1ed system but am certainly open to 2ed setting updates. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T07:58:01-07:00","id":1494864,"title":"","content":"Well first off, if you don't already have it, Predators. That book is almost essential. Everything you need to create some of the most terrifying monsters to hunt. The Rockies is only really needed if you plan to run that setting. That being said, it is pretty handy if you need some premade packs to interact with. The old demo is pretty cool. Great place to start if you want to get a feel for the game, especially if you want to use the Rockies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T11:30:24-07:00","id":1494878,"title":"","content":"I do have both Predators and Rockies. From what I recall Predators has the info on the rat and spider spirit hosts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T13:36:42-07:00","id":1494886,"title":"","content":"It does have info on the Hosts, yes. It also has an impressive amount of spirit write ups and rules for spirit Ridden. The final chapter of the book has write ups for these almost Lovecraftian horrors to server as the big bads for your game. It's an awesome book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T17:31:25-07:00","id":1495923,"title":"","content":"The demo is actually really good for trying the setting out. Plus it\u2019s free so if you don\u2019t like it than no loss. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s worth pointing out the uratha are revamped in second edition so they hit much harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T18:11:06-07:00","id":1495927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1494860-using-1ed-to-try-out-the-setting#post1494860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My group never really explored NWOD/COD after the OWOD ended. Over the years I did collect the majority of the WtF 1ed books as well as the other games. I want to run short campaigns for each of the COD settings to try them out. For WtF what books would you suggest to really focus on for a 1ed game? How useful is the Hunting Ground Rockies book in particular or the old demo campaign? As for 2ed, I have checked it out and system wise it's not my thing so I plan on using the 1ed system but am certainly open to 2ed setting updates. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1ed fluff is fantastic, but I advise you to use the 2e rules, those are far FAR better for nearly everything you might want to try. Totems are better fleshed out, XP costs, Humans, Wolf-Blooded, Hosts, everything.<br /> <br /> From 1ed just ignore the references to Unihar, and the rest would be portable to 2e.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}